@startuml

actor "User" as User
participant ":Search Page\n(Frontend)" as UI
participant ":PipelineStore\n(Zustand)" as Store
participant ":API Gateway\n(/topics)" as API
participant ":ProjectService" as PS
participant ":ProjectRepository" as PR
participant ":TopicModellingService" as TMS
participant ":JobQueueService" as JQS
participant ":reconciliation_task" as RT
participant ":LLMClient" as LLM
participant ":Ollama (LLM)" as Ollama
participant ":Redis\n(broker + result backend)" as Redis

autonumber

== Preconditions ==
note over User, UI
  User is authenticated, a project is active,
  and topic generation has completed (generated_topics exist,
  optionally edited/merged in the frontend).
end note

== Read Current Topics ==

UI -> Store : Read validated list[Topic] (generated, possibly edited)
Store --> UI : list[Topic]
UI --> User : Display current topic list

== Main Flow – Dispatch ==

User -> UI : Initiate topic reconciliation
UI -> Store : Read project_id + current list[Topic]
Store --> UI : project_id, list[Topic]

UI -> API : POST /topics/reconcile\n{ project_id, topics }
API -> API : get_current_user (verify bearer token)
API -> PS : verify_project_owner(project_id, user_id)
PS -> PR : find_by_id(project_id)
PR --> PS : Project | None
alt project missing or not owned
    PS --> API : raise ProjectNotFound / ProjectAccessDenied
    API --> UI : 404 / 403
end

API -> TMS : submit_reconciliation(project_id,\n[t.model_dump() for t in topics])
TMS -> JQS : dispatch("...reconciliation_task",\n{ project_id, topics })
JQS -> Redis : send_task (enqueue to broker)
JQS --> TMS : job_id (AsyncResult.id)
TMS --> API : job_id
API --> UI : { job_id }

UI -> Store : topicSubStep = "reconciling"\nStore reconciliationJobId
UI --> User : Show progress (Reconciling topics with the LLM...)

== SSE Progress Stream ==

UI -> API : GET /jobs/{job_id}/stream (SSE)
API -> JQS : stream_progress(job_id)

loop Until terminal state (poll every ~1s)
    JQS -> Redis : get_status -> Celery AsyncResult.state
    Redis --> JQS : PENDING / PROGRESS
    JQS --> API : JobStatus { status, progress, result }
    API --> UI : SSE event (JobStatus JSON)
    UI --> User : Update progress indicator
end

== Background Task Execution (Celery worker) ==

Redis -> RT : Worker picks up task
RT -> LLM : reconcile(list[Topic])

alt Ollama responds
    LLM -> Ollama : POST reconciliation prompt
    Ollama --> LLM : grouped topics JSON
    LLM -> LLM : Validate output, flatten surface ids ->\ngeneration-era origin_topic_ids,\npreserve any dropped topic
    LLM --> RT : reconciled list[Topic]\n(each with origin_topic_ids)
else Ollama unavailable / parse error
    LLM -> Ollama : POST reconciliation prompt
    Ollama --> LLM : (exception)
    LLM -> LLM : _fallback — return originals unchanged\n(new topic_ids, origin_topic_ids preserved)
    LLM --> RT : passthrough list[Topic]
    note right of LLM
      LLMClient.reconcile NEVER raises on LLM failure;
      it silently falls back. There is no LLM_UNAVAILABLE
      failure path — reconciliation still completes SUCCESS.
    end note
end

RT -> PS : update_reconciled_topics(project_id, reconciled)
PS -> PR : update_reconciled_topics(project_id, reconciled)
note right of PR
  $set pending_pipeline.reconciled_topics only.
  generated_topics and topic_mapping are preserved unchanged.
end note
PR --> PS : OK
PS --> RT : OK
RT -> Redis : task result =\nReconciliationResponse(topics)

== Completion ==

JQS -> Redis : get_status -> SUCCESS + result { topics }
JQS --> API : JobStatus { status: SUCCESS, result: { topics } }
API --> UI : SSE event (final)
UI -> Store : setReconciledTopics(result.topics)\ntopicSubStep = "reconciled"\n(generated_topics kept for revert)
Store --> UI : Reconciled topic list ready
UI --> User : Display reconciled topics\n(name, description, "Fuses: X + Y" from origin_topic_ids)

== Frontend-only Editing (no backend calls) ==

opt User edits / deletes / cancels (all local PipelineStore state)
    note over UI, Store
      - Edit reconciled topic name/description -> updateReconciledTopic
      - Delete reconciled topic -> splitReconciledTopic (re-expands origins)
      - Cancel -> cancelReconciliation: discard reconciled list,
        restore generated_topics as the active list.
      pending_pipeline.reconciled_topics in MongoDB is not modified
      by these local edits (only the next backend action persists).
    end note
end

== Accept / Skip ==

User -> UI : Accept reconciled topics (or "Skip to Labelling")
UI -> Store : Mark topic step complete\nActive list = reconciled (or generated if skipped)
Store --> UI : Classifier training step unlocked
UI --> User : Proceed to classifier training step

== Exception – Task Fails Unexpectedly ==

RT -> Redis : task state = FAILURE (+ error)
JQS --> API : JobStatus { status: FAILURE }
API --> UI : SSE event (final)
UI -> Store : topicSubStep = "generated"
UI --> User : Notify: reconciliation failed. Please try again.

@enduml
